# SRG-APP-000367-AU-000230  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to generate reports that support
# on-demand reporting requirements.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000367-AU-000230
group:           V-206500
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001879
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Splunk can define a report, dispatch it on a stated cycle, and deliver the
                 rendered result through the email alert action, which is what carries
                 report generation past ad hoc search into support for a reporting
                 requirement.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email in 1|true
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] action.email.sendpdf https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] schedule_window https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The reporting cycle, the recipients and the required report format are
                 organization-defined parameters recorded in the system security plan.
external:        Delivery of the report rests on the mail transfer agent, its credentials
                 and network reachability from the Splunk host, none of which is Splunk
                 configuration.
external:        The delivered form of a report, which is organization-defined and spread
                 across five savedsearches.conf switches and alert_actions.conf, so no
                 single key carries it.

citation:        savedsearches.conf.spec:44 search, :73 enableSched = [0|1] default 0, :79
                 cron_schedule, :193 schedule_window, :300 action.email = <boolean> default
                 false, :383 action.email.sendpdf = [1|0] default 0;
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:157 [email].
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: a report defined in
                 savedsearches.conf to satisfy an audit reporting requirement is not
                 dispatched (enableSched not 1 or no cron_schedule) or has no delivery
                 action configured, so the application is not configured to the fullest
                 extent it can contribute to this requirement.
